3127. Make a Square with the Same Color
Easy | Open on LeetCode
Input data: a 2D matrix grid of size 3 x 3 consisting only of characters 'B' and 'W'. Character 'W'
identifies the white color, and character 'B' identifies the black color. Goal: change the color of zero
or one cell so that the matrix has a 2 x 2 square where all cells are of the same color. Required
result: true if it is possible to create a 2 x 2 square of the same color, otherwise, produce
false..grid-container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 30px 30px 30px; padding: 10px;
}.grid-item { background-color: black; border: 1px solid gray; height: 30px; font-size: 30px;
text-align: center; }.grid-item-white { background-color: white; }
Constraints. grid.length == 3. grid[i].length == 3. grid[i][j] is either 'W' or 'B'.
